{"compatibility":"minor","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: minor.

Protected data: `X`.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

Changes: added `X_safestan_copy`, a deterministic top-level data copy with `X_safestan_copy[t, i] = X[t, i]`, so transformed-data computations of `g_bar` and `g_sigma` do not read protected `X` before it is observed. Added `sigma_matrix`, a deterministic transformed-data expansion of `sigma`, to express the likelihood as one top-level sampling statement. Replaced the row-wise `G[t] ~ lognormal(...)` prior with the equivalent vectorized `G ~ lognormal(...)`, and replaced the row-wise `X[t] ~ normal(...)` likelihood with the equivalent vectorized `X ~ normal(...)`. Added `F ~ dirichlet(rep_vector(1.0, I))` to make explicit the flat simplex prior implicit in the original constrained simplex parameter and satisfy SafeStan's unique-prior requirement.
","model_safe_stan":"// Evan Ira Blumgart (2012) Hamiltonian Monte Carlo Estimation of
// PM2.5 Source Apportionment and Related Health Effects.
// M.A. Dissertation.  Department of Statistics. 
// The University of Auckland.

data {
  int<lower=0> T;
  int<lower=0> I;
  int<lower=0> K;
  matrix<lower=0.0>[T, I] X;
  matrix<lower=0.0>[T, I] X_safestan_copy;
  array[I] real<lower=0> sigma;
}
transformed data {
  real<lower=0> g_bar;
  real<lower=0> g_sigma;
  vector[T] temp;
  matrix<lower=0>[T, I] sigma_matrix;
  for (t in 1 : T) {
    temp[t] = log(sum(X_safestan_copy[t]));
  }
  g_bar = mean(temp);
  g_sigma = sd(temp);
  for (t in 1 : T) {
    for (i in 1 : I) {
      sigma_matrix[t, i] = sigma[i];
    }
  }
}
parameters {
  matrix<lower=0>[T, K] G;
  array[K] simplex[I] F;
}
model {
  matrix[T, I] mu;
  G ~ lognormal(g_bar, g_sigma);
  F ~ dirichlet(rep_vector(1.0, I));
  for (t in 1 : T) {
    for (i in 1 : I) {
      mu[t, i] = 0;
      for (k in 1 : K) {
        mu[t, i] = mu[t, i] + G[t, k] * F[k, i];
      }
    }
  }
  X ~ normal(mu, sigma_matrix);
}
